  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Slide 7
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: 7. Bridge wire should be of the uniform area of cross-section because
    we assume that resistance is proportional to the length of the wire while deriving
    the formula, which will be true only when the wire is of the uniform cross-sectional
    area throughout.
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: "Applying balanced Wheatstone bridge condition:\r\n\r\nP / Q =
    Resistance (Resistance (AJ)) / Resistance (Resistance (JB))\r\n      (as uniform
    wire)\r\n\r\nP / Q = AJ / JB = l\u2081 / l\u2082"
  options:
  - True
  - False
  - Cannot be determined
  - Both True and False
  correctOptionIndex: 0
